<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan April gold imports up 0.98 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Taiwan April gold imports up 0.98 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's imports of gold bars, coins and plate increased 0.98 percent to 9.941 tonnes in April from 9.844 tonnes a year earlier, the Finance Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Traders attributed the modest April import to Taiwan's traditionally slow gold buying season from March to early October.</p>
<p>&quot;Gold buying would remain slow in the coming few months,&quot; a Taipei gold trader said.</p>
<p>The ministry said Taiwan's gold exports in April remained modest at 0.286 tonnes, up from 0.197 tonnes April 1996.</p>
<p>Main Taiwan April gold suppliers were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Country	     April 1997	   April 1996</p>
<p>  Swiss		 0.580		   4.258</p>
<p>  South Korea	 1.202		   1.555</p>
<p>  British	     0.788		   0.000</p>
<p>  Canada		3.698		   0.200</p>
<p>  U.S.A.		1.205		   0.002</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
